&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How we&#39;re different&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe that the highest-impact AI research will be big science. At Anthropic we work as a single cohesive team on just a few large-scale research efforts. And we value impact — advancing our long-term goals of steerable, trustworthy AI — rather than work on smaller and more specific puzzles. We view AI research as an empirical science, which has as much in common with physics and biology as with traditional efforts in computer science. We&#39;re an extremely collaborative group, and we host frequent research discussions to ensure that we are pursuing the highest-impact work at any given time. As such, we greatly value communication skills.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The easiest way to understand our research directions is to read our recent research. This research continues many of the directions our team worked on prior to Anthropic, including: GPT-3, Circuit-Based Interpretability, Multimodal Neurons, Scaling Laws, AI &amp;amp; Compute, Concrete Problems in AI Safety, and Learning from Human Preferences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Come work with us!&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anthropic is a public benefit corporation headquartered in San Francisco. We offer competitive compensation and benefits, optional equity donation matching, generous vacation and parental leave, flexible working hours, and a lovely office space in which to collaborate with colleagues. &lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Guidance on Candidates&#39; AI Usage:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Learn about&amp;nbsp;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link&quot; href=&quot;https://www.anthropic.com/candidate-ai-guidance&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://www.anthropic.com/candidate-ai-guidance&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;our policy&lt;/a&gt; for using AI in our application process.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;GitLab is the intelligent orchestration platform for DevSecOps. GitLab enables organizations to increase developer productivity, improve operational efficiency, reduce security and compliance risk, and accelerate digital transformation. More than 50 million registered users and more than 50% of the Fortune 100* trust GitLab to ship better, more secure software faster.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The same principles built into our products are reflected in how our team works: we embrace AI as a core productivity multiplier, with all team members expected to incorporate AI into their daily workflows to drive efficiency, innovation, and impact. GitLab is where careers accelerate, innovation flourishes, and every voice is valued. Our high-performance culture is driven by our values&amp;nbsp;and continuous knowledge exchange, enabling our team members to reach their full potential while collaborating with industry leaders to solve complex problems. &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OuZIb5zszQI&quot;&gt;Co-create the future with us&lt;/a&gt; as we build technology that transforms how the world develops software.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;*&lt;em&gt;Fortune 500® is a registered trademark of Fortune Media IP Limited, used under license. Claim based on GitLab data. Fortune 100 refers to the top 20% ranked companies in the 2025 Fortune 500 list, published in June 2025. Fortune and Fortune Media IP Limited are not affiliated with, and do not endorse products or services of GitLab.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;An overview of this role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Director, Social Media, you&#39;ll lead GitLab&#39;s global social media strategy and help people understand how GitLab is co-creating the future of software development. The role shapes how GitLab shows up across social channels, connecting our company, product, and employer stories, to build meaningful engagement with customers, users, contributors, candidates, and industry audiences. Expect to set clear priorities, guide execution, and use insights to strengthen GitLab&#39;s voice and business impact. You&#39;ll own the outcomes of GitLab&#39;s social function — strategy, budget, team development, tooling, and results — and serve as GitLab&#39;s senior-most voice on social strategy with executive stakeholders.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a player-coach role. You&#39;ll set the strategy and stay close enough to the work to write, build, and ship alongside the team. Two Social Media Managers report to the head of corporate communication and work with you on a dotted-line basis. You&#39;ll set their strategic direction, raise the editorial and craft bar, and develop them as practitioners, including goal-setting, feedback, and career development in partnership with their manager. Influence matters in this role, which is why it calls for someone who has already led and grown social practitioners.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the performance of GitLab&#39;s social function and its contribution to marketing and business goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead GitLab&#39;s global organic social media strategy, channel plans, and editorial priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own GitLab&#39;s YouTube strategy end to end — channel architecture, programming and series development, long- and short-form video, packaging (titles, thumbnails, metadata), search and recommendation optimization, and subscriber and watch-time growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Growth Marketing on paid social, including briefing creative, aligning organic and paid on shared audiences and messaging, informing boosting and amplification decisions, and connecting paid performance back to organic strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop clear, audience-focused campaigns that support company, product, brand, and talent goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Guide content planning and publishing across social channels while maintaining a consistent GitLab voice.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the social media budget, tooling stack, and agency, freelance, and production partner relationships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with teams across Marketing, Communications, Product, Sales, Talent Acquisition, and other functions to plan and deliver social programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build processes that support effective collaboration in GitLab&#39;s all-remote, asynchronous environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use social listening, audience insights, and performance data to improve content and inform broader marketing decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the measurement framework for social — KPIs, dashboards, and reporting cadence — and report performance and learnings to marketing and executive leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with DevRel on community engagement to help GitLab participate in relevant industry conversations with a clear, useful point of view.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and run creator, influencer, and advocacy programs, including developer creators, GitLab community contributors, and team member advocacy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own GitLab&#39;s employee advocacy program — grow participation across Marketing, Sales, Engineering, and Talent, equip team members with content worth sharing, and measure reach, engagement, and contribution to brand and talent goals. Partner with Communications and Talent Acquisition on enablement, and manage the advocacy platform and its adoption.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support executive and expert social presence, partnering with Communications to help GitLab leaders and technical experts show up credibly on social, including constructive conversations with C-suite executives about proposed content.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply AI tools thoughtfully across the social workflow to help GitLab model what an AI-native marketing team looks like.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare for and guide responses to sensitive or fast-moving issues in partnership with the appropriate teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years in social media, including at least 5 years leading social strategy for a global brand at the senior manager level or above, and accountable for the function&#39;s results.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience owning a social function end to end, including strategy, budget, headcount, tooling, and results as the accountable leader.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading teams, agencies, and cross-functional programs, with clear ownership of and accountability for outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Depth in YouTube strategy, including owning and growing a brand or business channel, and can speak to programming decisions, video formats, packaging, and the metrics that actually move a channel.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience growing LinkedIn and X as primary channels, with judgment about what content, format, and cadence work on each.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with paid social programs and how organic and paid social reinforce each other, including creative for paid, audience strategy, and interpreting paid performance data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience connecting social media programs to broader brand, communications, product, or business priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong editorial judgment and the ability to turn complex topics into clear, engaging content.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency with short-form and long-form video as core social formats, including working with production partners and creators.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience defining a measurement framework for social, including KPIs, dashboards, and reporting cadence, and presenting performance, learnings, and recommendations to executive leadership on a standing basis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building or scaling an employee advocacy program, including driving adoption across multiple functions, sustaining participation beyond launch, and reporting attributed reach and business contribution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency with an enterprise social stack for publishing, listening, and advocacy. Ours is Sprout Social, Meltwater, and EveryoneSocial.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience running social programs across multiple regions and languages, and judgment about what to localize versus centralize.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Skill in managing multiple priorities and making sound decisions in fast-moving situations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A collaborative, inclusive approach and the ability to work effectively in a distributed, asynchronous environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passion about GitLab&#39;s mission and the future of software development, open source, artificial intelligence, and DevSecOps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is part of GitLab&#39;s Marketing organization and works across teams to present a clear, consistent company voice on social media. The team collaborates asynchronously with partners across regions and functions, balancing planned campaigns with timely engagement. Together, you&#39;ll help audiences understand GitLab&#39;s platform, mission, values, and impact.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;The base salary range for this role’s listed level is currently for residents of the&amp;nbsp;United States only. This range is intended to reflect the role&#39;s base salary rate in locations throughout the US.&amp;nbsp;Grade level and salary ranges are determined through interviews and a review of education, experience, knowledge, skills, abilities of the applicant, equity with other team members, alignment with market data,&amp;nbsp;and geographic location.&amp;nbsp;The base salary range does not include any bonuses, equity, or benefits. See more information on our &lt;a class=&quot;waffle-rich-text-link&quot; href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/total-rewards/benefits/general-and-entity-benefits/&quot; data-sheets-formula-bar-text-link=&quot;https://bit.ly/GLBeneUS&quot; data-sheets-formula-bar-text-style=&quot;font-size:12px;color:#1155cc;font-weight:normal;text-decoration:underline;font-family:&#39;&#39;Arial&#39;&#39;;font-style:normal;text-decoration-skip-ink:none;&quot;&gt;benefits&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-formula-bar-text-style=&quot;font-size:12px;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;text-decoration:none;font-family:&#39;Arial&#39;;font-style:normal;text-decoration-skip-ink:none;&quot;&gt; and &lt;/span&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;waffle-rich-text-link&quot; href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/stock-options/&quot; data-sheets-formula-bar-text-link=&quot;https://bit.ly/GLequity&quot; data-sheets-formula-bar-text-style=&quot;font-size:12px;color:#1155cc;font-weight:normal;text-decoration:underline;font-family:&#39;&#39;Arial&#39;&#39;;font-style:normal;text-decoration-skip-ink:none;&quot;&gt;equity&lt;/a&gt;. Sales roles are also eligible for incentive pay targeted at up to 100% of the offered base salary.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;United States Salary Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$139,200&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$235,200 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How GitLab Supports Full-Time Employees&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/total-rewards/benefits/general-and-entity-benefits/&quot;&gt;Benefits to support your health, finances, and well-being&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/people-group/time-off-and-absence/time-off-types/#flexible-paid-time-off-pto&quot;&gt;Flexible Paid Time Off&amp;nbsp;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/company/culture/inclusion/tmrg-tmag/&quot;&gt;Team Member Resource Groups&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/total-rewards/stock-options/&quot;&gt;Equity Compensation &amp;amp; Employee Stock Purchase Plan&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/people-group/learning-and-development/growth-and-development/&quot;&gt;Growth and Development Fund&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/total-rewards/benefits/general-and-entity-benefits/#parental-leave&quot;&gt;Parental Leave&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please note that we welcome interest from candidates with varying levels of experience; many successful candidates do not meet every single requirement. Additionally, studies have shown that people from &lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/company/culture/inclusion/#examples-of-select-underrepresented-groups&quot;&gt;underrepresented groups&lt;/a&gt; are less likely to apply to a job unless they meet every single qualification. If you&#39;re excited about this role, please apply and allow our recruiters to assess your application.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Country Hiring Guidelines: &lt;/strong&gt;GitLab hires new team members in countries around the world. All of our roles are remote, however some roles may carry specific location-based eligibility requirements. Our Talent Acquisition team can help answer any questions about location after starting the recruiting process.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Privacy Policy: &lt;/strong&gt;Please review our &lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/hiring/candidate-faq/recruitment-privacy-policy/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Recruitment Privacy Policy.&lt;/a&gt; Your privacy is important to us.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;GitLab is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and is an affirmative action employer. GitLab’s policies and practices relating to recruitment, employment, career development and advancement, promotion, and retirement are based solely on merit, regardless of race, color, religion, ancestry, sex (including pregnancy, lactation, sexual orientation, gender identity, or gender expression), national origin, age, citizenship, marital status, mental or physical disability, genetic information (including family medical history), discharge status from the military, protected veteran status (which includes disabled veterans, recently separated veterans, active duty wartime or campaign badge veterans, and Armed Forces service medal veterans), or any other basis protected by law. GitLab will not tolerate discrimination or harassment based on any of these characteristics. See also&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/people-policies/inc-usa/#equal-employment-opportunity-policy&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;GitLab’s EEO Policy&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/labor-and-employment-notices/#eeoc-us-equal-employment-opportunity-commission-notices&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;EEO is the Law&lt;/a&gt;. If you have a disability or special need that requires&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/people-policies/inc-usa/#reasonable-accommodation&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;accommodation&lt;/a&gt;, please let us know during the&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/hiring/interviewing/#adjustments-to-our-interview-process&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;recruiting process&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Anthropic&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anthropic’s mission is to create reliable, interpretable, and steerable AI systems. We want AI to be safe and beneficial for our users and for society as a whole. Our team is a quickly growing group of committed researchers, engineers, policy experts, and business leaders working together to build beneficial AI systems.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;About the role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an AV Engineer focused on builds and design, you&#39;ll design and implement the systems that enable world-class collaboration and communication across offices. This role is critical as we rapidly expand our physical footprint, with plans for multiple new offices and expansions over the coming years.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll be responsible for architecting AV solutions from concept through commissioning, ensuring our conference rooms, event spaces, and collaboration areas provide frictionless experiences that enable our teams to advance AI safety research. You&#39;ll help establish standards and systems that scale efficiently while pushing the boundaries of what&#39;s possible in workplace collaboration technology.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is an opportunity to shape how a cutting-edge AI research organization communicates and collaborates, building infrastructure that supports everything from small team meetings to company-wide all-hands broadcasts reaching thousands of remote participants.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead AV design, procurement, and programming for new office builds, expansions, and retrofits across our global portfolio&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create and maintain AV system designs including schematic drawings, line diagrams, and elevation plans&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Program and commission AV systems to meet specific use cases and user requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Execute successful &quot;first day of business&quot; deployments for new offices, ensuring all systems are operational for day-one occupancy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Attend build coordination meetings with architects, contractors, and workplace teams to drive AV requirements and integration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Innovate and test emerging AV technologies to optimize productivity and enable premium experiences for existing and upcoming spaces&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop automated solutions to improve system reliability and reduce operational overhead&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Security and IT teams to ensure AV systems meet enterprise security requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create comprehensive documentation for all systems including programming logic, troubleshooting guides, and operational procedures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee operations globally to ensure seamless AV operations and service delivery standards are consistently met&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage relationships with AV integrators and vendors to ensure project success&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist with AV operations support including event production and system maintenance as needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;You may be a good fit if you&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have 8+ years of experience designing and implementing AV systems in an enterprise environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are proficient in control system programming utilizing the Q-Sys ecosystem or similar&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have hands-on experience with video conferencing platforms, particularly Google Meet&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Can read and create AV technical drawings including schematics, line diagrams, and rack elevations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand digital signal processing (DSP) concepts for audio, including acoustic echo cancellation, noise reduction, EQ/dynamics, and automixing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are familiar with enterprise video distribution, streaming technologies, and broadcast standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Can manage multiple projects simultaneously while meeting aggressive timelines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate effectively with non-technical stakeholders to translate requirements into technical solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have excellent troubleshooting skills and are comfortable diving into complex integrated systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Care about creating exceptional user experiences through technology&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are excited about the opportunity to build scalable AV infrastructure from the ground up&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Strong candidates may also have&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Logitech video conferencing ecosystem and management platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Certifications such as Q-Sys Level 2, CTS, or CTS-D&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with control scripts using Lua within Q-Sys&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in broadcast production or live event engineering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Netgear network switches running AV over IP systems (QLAN, Dante, SMPTE 2110)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with digital signage platforms (Appspace or similar)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of acoustical design principles for conference spaces&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of successful large-scale office technology deployments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous experience performing AV installations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background working in high-growth technology companies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Google Workspace administration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Role Specific Location Policy:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This role will be based in our San Francisco office&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This role is expected to be in office 75% of the time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This position will require up to 8 weeks of domestic and international travel to help with new office build outs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Deadline to apply: None. Applications will be received on a rolling basis.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;The annual compensation range for this role is listed below.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For sales roles, the range provided is the role’s On Target Earnings (&quot;OTE&quot;) range, meaning that the range includes both the sales commissions/sales bonuses target and annual base salary for the role.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Annual Salary:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$285,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$325,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Logistics&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum education: &lt;/strong&gt;Bachelor’s degree or an equivalent combination of education, training, and/or experience&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required field of study:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;A field relevant to the role as demonstrated through coursework, training, or professional experience&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum years of experience: &lt;/strong&gt;Years of experience required will correlate with the internal job level requirements for the position&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location-based hybrid policy:&lt;/strong&gt; Currently, we expect all staff to be in one of our offices at least 25% of the time. However, some roles may require more time in our offices.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Visa sponsorship:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;We do sponsor visas! However, we aren&#39;t able to successfully sponsor visas for every role and every candidate. But if we make you an offer, we will make every reasonable effort to get you a visa, and we retain an immigration lawyer to help with this.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We encourage you to apply even if you do not believe you meet every single qualification.&lt;/strong&gt; Not all strong candidates will meet every single qualification as listed.&amp;nbsp; Research shows that people who identify as being from underrepresented groups are more prone to experiencing imposter syndrome and doubting the strength of their candidacy, so we urge you not to exclude yourself prematurely and to submit an application if you&#39;re interested in this work. We think AI systems like the ones we&#39;re building have enormous social and ethical implications. We think this makes representation even more important, and we strive to include a range of diverse perspectives on our team.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Your safety matters to us.&lt;/strong&gt; To protect yourself from potential scams, remember that Anthropic recruiters only contact you from&amp;nbsp;@anthropic.com&amp;nbsp;email addresses. In some cases, we may partner with vetted recruiting agencies who will identify themselves as working on behalf of Anthropic. Be cautious of emails from other domains. Legitimate Anthropic recruiters will never ask for money, fees, or banking information before your first day. If you&#39;re ever unsure about a communication, don&#39;t click any links—visit&amp;nbsp;&lt;u data-stringify-type=&quot;underline&quot;&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link c-link--underline&quot; href=&quot;http://anthropic.com/careers&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;http://anthropic.com/careers&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot; data-remove-tab-index=&quot;true&quot;&gt;anthropic.com/careers&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&amp;nbsp;directly for confirmed position openings.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How we&#39;re different&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe that the highest-impact AI research will be big science. At Anthropic we work as a single cohesive team on just a few large-scale research efforts. And we value impact — advancing our long-term goals of steerable, trustworthy AI — rather than work on smaller and more specific puzzles. We view AI research as an empirical science, which has as much in common with physics and biology as with traditional efforts in computer science. We&#39;re an extremely collaborative group, and we host frequent research discussions to ensure that we are pursuing the highest-impact work at any given time. As such, we greatly value communication skills.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The easiest way to understand our research directions is to read our recent research. This research continues many of the directions our team worked on prior to Anthropic, including: GPT-3, Circuit-Based Interpretability, Multimodal Neurons, Scaling Laws, AI &amp;amp; Compute, Concrete Problems in AI Safety, and Learning from Human Preferences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Come work with us!&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anthropic is a public benefit corporation headquartered in San Francisco. We offer competitive compensation and benefits, optional equity donation matching, generous vacation and parental leave, flexible working hours, and a lovely office space in which to collaborate with colleagues. &lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Guidance on Candidates&#39; AI Usage:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Learn about&amp;nbsp;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link&quot; href=&quot;https://www.anthropic.com/candidate-ai-guidance&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://www.anthropic.com/candidate-ai-guidance&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;our policy&lt;/a&gt; for using AI in our application process.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Anthropic&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anthropic’s mission is to create reliable, interpretable, and steerable AI systems. We want AI to be safe and beneficial for our users and for society as a whole. Our team is a quickly growing group of committed researchers, engineers, policy experts, and business leaders working together to build beneficial AI systems.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anthropic is scaling compute internationally — growing our footprint in new countries. We&#39;re hiring a Country Lead to be the single, accountable owner of our compute strategy in Canada: the person who leads a team of cross-functional experts driving site selection, leasing, energy, financing, government relations and policy, community engagement, construction, and operations. This person will be ultimately responsible for bringing gigawatts of compute online in Canada.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You won&#39;t build this alone. The specialist functions — leasing, energy, policy, construction, finance — are hired and managed centrally by functional leads based in San Francisco. Your job is to provide cross-functional leadership over that team in-country: coordinating and driving accountability across workstreams, while representing Anthropic externally with government and industry counterparts in Canada.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a high-ambiguity, high-trust role for someone who can bring structure to a fast-growing, cross-functional effort without needing formal authority to do it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Own the end-to-end strategy and coordination for Anthropic&#39;s compute build-out in Canada, from initial site selection through construction and operations. While each component will be run by subject matter experts, this role will act as the overall leader and coordinator of that team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Serve as the primary point of accountability for cross-functional workstreams; leasing, financing, energy, government relations/policy, community engagement, construction, and operations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Provide working leadership to the in-country cross-functional team, driving alignment and unblocking issues.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Represent Anthropic with government officials, utilities, energy providers, and other external stakeholders in Canada.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Build and maintain relationships within the Canadian government and the energy industry to support site, power, and policy outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Track progress and surface risks across parallel workstreams as the country&#39;s compute footprint scales from initial sites to multiple gigawatts.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Translate between Anthropic&#39;s global compute priorities and the specific regulatory, political, and market conditions in Canada.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Canadian national with established links into government and the energy industry strongly preferred.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Structured thinker with a track record of learning new domains quickly and going deep fast.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Excellent communicator, comfortable representing Anthropic to senior government, utility, and industry stakeholders.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Demonstrated ability to lead and coordinate cross-functional teams without direct line authority.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Hyper-organized and detail-oriented, with the ability to own multiple concurrent workstreams at once.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Comfortable with ambiguity; a problem solver who drives structure into undefined situations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Background in energy, infrastructure, or a related sector.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Prior experience with large-scale infrastructure or datacenter development.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Existing relationships with Canadian federal or provincial government bodies relevant to energy, land use, or industrial development.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience managing or overseeing capital-intensive projects.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Familiarity with the compute, cloud, or datacenter industry.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Logistics&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum education: &lt;/strong&gt;Bachelor’s degree or an equivalent combination of education, training, and/or experience&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required field of study:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;A field relevant to the role as demonstrated through coursework, training, or professional experience&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum years of experience: &lt;/strong&gt;Years of experience required will correlate with the internal job level requirements for the position&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location-based hybrid policy:&lt;/strong&gt; Currently, we expect all staff to be in one of our offices at least 25% of the time. However, some roles may require more time in our offices.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Visa sponsorship:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;We do sponsor visas! However, we aren&#39;t able to successfully sponsor visas for every role and every candidate. But if we make you an offer, we will make every reasonable effort to get you a visa, and we retain an immigration lawyer to help with this.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We encourage you to apply even if you do not believe you meet every single qualification.&lt;/strong&gt; Not all strong candidates will meet every single qualification as listed.&amp;nbsp; Research shows that people who identify as being from underrepresented groups are more prone to experiencing imposter syndrome and doubting the strength of their candidacy, so we urge you not to exclude yourself prematurely and to submit an application if you&#39;re interested in this work. We think AI systems like the ones we&#39;re building have enormous social and ethical implications. We think this makes representation even more important, and we strive to include a range of diverse perspectives on our team.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Your safety matters to us.&lt;/strong&gt; To protect yourself from potential scams, remember that Anthropic recruiters only contact you from&amp;nbsp;@anthropic.com&amp;nbsp;email addresses. In some cases, we may partner with vetted recruiting agencies who will identify themselves as working on behalf of Anthropic. Be cautious of emails from other domains. Legitimate Anthropic recruiters will never ask for money, fees, or banking information before your first day. If you&#39;re ever unsure about a communication, don&#39;t click any links—visit&amp;nbsp;&lt;u data-stringify-type=&quot;underline&quot;&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link c-link--underline&quot; href=&quot;http://anthropic.com/careers&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;http://anthropic.com/careers&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot; data-remove-tab-index=&quot;true&quot;&gt;anthropic.com/careers&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&amp;nbsp;directly for confirmed position openings.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How we&#39;re different&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe that the highest-impact AI research will be big science. At Anthropic we work as a single cohesive team on just a few large-scale research efforts. And we value impact — advancing our long-term goals of steerable, trustworthy AI — rather than work on smaller and more specific puzzles. We view AI research as an empirical science, which has as much in common with physics and biology as with traditional efforts in computer science. We&#39;re an extremely collaborative group, and we host frequent research discussions to ensure that we are pursuing the highest-impact work at any given time. As such, we greatly value communication skills.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The easiest way to understand our research directions is to read our recent research. This research continues many of the directions our team worked on prior to Anthropic, including: GPT-3, Circuit-Based Interpretability, Multimodal Neurons, Scaling Laws, AI &amp;amp; Compute, Concrete Problems in AI Safety, and Learning from Human Preferences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Come work with us!&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anthropic is a public benefit corporation headquartered in San Francisco. We offer competitive compensation and benefits, optional equity donation matching, generous vacation and parental leave, flexible working hours, and a lovely office space in which to collaborate with colleagues. &lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Guidance on Candidates&#39; AI Usage:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Learn about&amp;nbsp;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link&quot; href=&quot;https://www.anthropic.com/candidate-ai-guidance&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://www.anthropic.com/candidate-ai-guidance&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;our policy&lt;/a&gt; for using AI in our application process.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Anthropic&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anthropic’s mission is to create reliable, interpretable, and steerable AI systems. We want AI to be safe and beneficial for our users and for society as a whole. Our team is a quickly growing group of committed researchers, engineers, policy experts, and business leaders working together to build beneficial AI systems.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;About the role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the Content Strategy Lead for Executive Programs, you will own what Anthropic brings to the table when we sit down with senior leaders from our most strategic customers. That covers Executive Briefings, Customer Advisory Boards, Executive Councils, and the other small-room gatherings where a C-level audience meets with our leaders, product teams, and researchers. You will set the content strategy across these programs, build the library of modules and the bench of speakers, and lead the team that keeps our content fresh as our models and products evolve.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role works cross-functionally with Product &amp;amp; Solutions Marketing, who owns positioning and messaging across industries and products, and customer programs which owns each program&#39;s operations, intake, and customer experience. You own the layer in between: turning Anthropic&#39;s product, research, and policy story into sessions built for an executive audience, deciding who is best placed to deliver them, and designing interactive formats and demos that work for customers building on the frontier.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The right candidate has a product marketing or narrative background, has built content for C-level customer audiences at an enterprise technology company, and has managed a team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 style=&quot;line-height: 2;&quot;&gt;Key responsibilities&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 2;&quot;&gt;Set and execute the content strategy across Executive Briefings, Customer Advisory Boards, Executive Councils, and other gatherings of strategic customers: the themes for the year, the narrative that connects them, and how content differs by program, audience, and purpose.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 2;&quot;&gt;Build and maintain an evergreen library of content modules that program leads and account teams can assemble into an agenda without starting from scratch. Modules span product and roadmap, research, safety and policy, industry and use-case sessions, demos, and discussion guides.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 2;&quot;&gt;Keep the library current. Set a refresh cadence tied to model and product launches, retire what is stale, maintain a pipeline of net-new content modules, and make sure nothing in front of a customer executive is out of date.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 2;&quot;&gt;Identify, recruit, develop and certify speakers from Anthropic&#39;s executive, product, research, and go-to-market teams. Maintain the cross-program roster, shape each speaker&#39;s session, and prepare them for the room.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 2;&quot;&gt;Design the experience, not only the presentation. Choose the format that fits the audience and the goal, whether that is a working session, a live demo, a conversation with a researcher, or a peer discussion among customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 2;&quot;&gt;Partner with program leads on agendas for the highest-priority engagements, tailoring modules to the customer&#39;s objectives. Set the standards and templates that let every other engagement meet the same bar.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 2;&quot;&gt;Work with Product &amp;amp; Solutions Marketing, Product, and Research so that executive-level content is ready when a launch happens, not weeks after.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 2;&quot;&gt;Capture what customers say in these rooms, including themes, objections, and requests. Route it to Product, Research, Marketing, and go-to-market leadership, and use it to improve the content.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 2;&quot;&gt;Measure what works, including session feedback, module usage, and speaker performance, and work with program leads to connect content to program outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 2;&quot;&gt;Hire, manage, and develop the team responsible for executive program content, and set its quality bar.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 2;&quot;&gt;Use Claude to scale the work: build workflows that tailor modules to a customer&#39;s industry and priorities so a customized session does not require a rebuild.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 style=&quot;line-height: 2;&quot;&gt;Minimum qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 2;&quot;&gt;Built content for C-level customer audiences in executive briefings, advisory boards, executive councils, or similar programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 2;&quot;&gt;Built a content system that other people rely on, such as a module library, a session catalog, or a speaker program, and kept it current through frequent product change.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 2;&quot;&gt;The technical fluency to work directly with researchers and engineers, understand what they have built, and explain it accurately to a business executive.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 2;&quot;&gt;Experience coaching senior executives and technical experts as speakers, including giving direct feedback on their material.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 2;&quot;&gt;Judgment about format: you know when a room needs a presentation, a demo, or a facilitated discussion, and you can design each one.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 2;&quot;&gt;Experience managing people, including hiring and developing a team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 2;&quot;&gt;A high bar for writing. You can draft an executive session narrative yourself and improve one written by someone else.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 2;&quot;&gt;Genuine interest in AI and in helping the world&#39;s largest enterprises adopt it responsibly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 style=&quot;line-height: 2;&quot;&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 2;&quot;&gt;12+ years in product marketing, executive content, or executive customer programs at a B2B technology company. You have owned positioning and messaging for a technical product and know how to adapt it for different audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 2;&quot;&gt;Experience at a company where the product changes quickly and content has a short shelf life.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 2;&quot;&gt;Hands-on experience using AI tools to produce or tailor content.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 2;&quot;&gt;Experience facilitating executive discussions, not only preparing others to lead them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 2;&quot;&gt;Worked with customers in regulated industries such as financial services, healthcare, or the public sector.&lt;/li&gt;
