&lt;p&gt;Anthropic’s mission is to create reliable, interpretable, and steerable AI systems. We want AI to be safe and beneficial for our users and for society as a whole. Our team is a quickly growing group of committed researchers, engineers, policy experts, and business leaders working together to build beneficial AI systems.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Applied AI Solutions Architect supporting a dedicated national security mission program, you will be the customer&#39;s trusted technical advisor — helping them understand the value of Claude and how to successfully integrate and deploy it into their technology stack. You&#39;ll combine deep technical and cyber domain expertise with customer-facing skills to architect LLM solutions for complex mission challenges while maintaining our high standards for safety and reliability. Working closely with our Sales, Product, and Engineering teams, you&#39;ll guide the customer from technical discovery through successful deployment, much of it on-site in secure environments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the dedicated technical advisor for one or more national security mission programs, from discovery and evaluation through deployment and adoption&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the customer building with Claude Code, the Claude API, and Claude for Enterprise&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help develop evaluation frameworks to measure Claude&#39;s performance for mission-specific use cases&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Guide technical architecture decisions and integration into the customer&#39;s existing stack&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate internally across Sales, Product, and Engineering to drive customer success&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create and deliver technical content from engineering deep dives to executive briefings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work primarily on-site with the customer&#39;s engineering and mission teams in secure government facilities, while maintaining close internal coordination and feedback with Anthropic’s Applied AI and Engineering teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Active TS/SCI clearance with Polygraph&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience working within US intelligence community agencies as a government civilian or cleared contractor&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in technical customer-facing roles (solutions architecture, sales engineering, or similar)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional ability to communicate technical concepts to diverse stakeholders, from engineers to executives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on expertise in one or more of the following domains: offensive or defensive cyber operations (including vulnerability research, reverse engineering, and ICS/OT security), cryptography and cryptanalysis, intelligence analysis and ISR (all-source, SIGINT, GEOINT), mission and weapons systems (command and control, space, electronic warfare, autonomy), CBRN and nonproliferation, or accreditation of classified systems (RMF, ATO, cross-domain solutions).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
