&lt;p&gt;GitLab is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and is an affirmative action employer. GitLab’s policies and practices relating to recruitment, employment, career development and advancement, promotion, and retirement are based solely on merit, regardless of race, color, religion, ancestry, sex (including pregnancy, lactation, sexual orientation, gender identity, or gender expression), national origin, age, citizenship, marital status, mental or physical disability, genetic information (including family medical history), discharge status from the military, protected veteran status (which includes disabled veterans, recently separated veterans, active duty wartime or campaign badge veterans, and Armed Forces service medal veterans), or any other basis protected by law. GitLab will not tolerate discrimination or harassment based on any of these characteristics. See also&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/people-policies/inc-usa/#equal-employment-opportunity-policy&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;GitLab’s EEO Policy&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/labor-and-employment-notices/#eeoc-us-equal-employment-opportunity-commission-notices&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;EEO is the Law&lt;/a&gt;. If you have a disability or special need that requires&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/people-policies/inc-usa/#reasonable-accommodation&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;accommodation&lt;/a&gt;, please let us know during the&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/hiring/interviewing/#adjustments-to-our-interview-process&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;recruiting process&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Anthropic&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anthropic’s mission is to create reliable, interpretable, and steerable AI systems. We want AI to be safe and beneficial for our users and for society as a whole. Our team is a quickly growing group of committed researchers, engineers, policy experts, and business leaders working together to build beneficial AI systems.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;About the role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anthropic&#39;s go-to-market engine runs on Salesforce: how leads become pipeline, how deals are tracked and forecast, how customers renew and expand, and how partners work alongside our sellers. As a Business Systems Analyst, you&#39;ll be responsible for how one of those core motions is represented in system, and a trusted partner to GTM leadership when they want to change how it works.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who operates at the intersection of three things: a strategist who can sit with GTM leaders and shape how they want to understand their part of the business, an analyst who can turn that into rigorous process and data design, and a builder who&#39;s comfortable enough in Salesforce to ship meaningful parts of it themselves. You can move fluidly between whiteboard, requirements doc, and admin console. You&#39;ll partner deeply with RevOps on the operating model and with our Salesforce developers on anything that needs code.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Where you might sit&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re hiring across several parts of the customer lifecycle. Placement depends on your background and where you can have the most impact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Opportunity Acceleration:&lt;/strong&gt; Owns how deals are tracked, forecast, and credited in Salesforce, from stage design and forecasting to the ownership and team structures behind them. You&#39;ll partner with sales leadership to make pipeline something everyone can trust and sellers can work quickly.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead-to-Pipeline:&lt;/strong&gt; Owns how leads, inbound demand, and BDR outreach become qualified pipeline: lifecycle stages, routing and ownership, handoff rules, and the tools BDRs and sellers work in every day. You&#39;ll partner with BDR, marketing, and sales leadership to make the path from first touch to open opportunity faster and easier to measure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Post-Sales:&lt;/strong&gt; Owns the systems behind renewals, expansion, and customer coverage: how post-sale opportunities are created, forecast, and worked by account management and customer success. You&#39;ll give post-sales leaders a clear, trustworthy view of the customer base and the tools to act on it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Partnerships:&lt;/strong&gt; Owns how partner-sourced and co-sell deals are registered, attributed, and worked alongside our sellers, including the partner-facing processes and reporting leadership relies on. You&#39;ll help turn a fast-growing channel into a motion the business can measure and scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Key responsibilities&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Own the design of your core funnel domain in Salesforce: lifecycle stages, process, exit and handoff criteria, key fields, and the automation and guardrails that keep the data trustworthy&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Partner with GTM leadership on how their motion runs and how they want to see it, and make the tradeoff calls on what teams enter versus what insight that data unlocks&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Partner with RevOps to systematize how GTM teams are structured, assigned, and credited: ownership, routing, coverage, splits, and the territory and role structures those depend on&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Operationalize the methodology in system, turning frameworks and process discipline into fields, validation, scoring, and in-context guidance that people actually use&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Act as data-model steward for your domain and its closest neighbors: the named approver for new fields, automation, and integrations touching those objects, and the keeper of why each one exists&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Build and ship declarative solutions yourself where that&#39;s the right call, and write specs clean enough that our developers can build the rest without five rounds of clarification&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Own the seams to the neighboring stages of the customer lifecycle (lead handoff, opportunity, quote-to-cash, renewal, partner attribution) so the experience is coherent end to end even where the build sits with another team&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Evaluate and configure tooling that accelerates the motion: routing, activity capture, sequencing, deal inspection, account planning&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Run discovery, UAT, enablement, and adoption measurement for everything you ship; help raise the bar for how BSA work is done on this team&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Minimum qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience in GTM/Revenue systems as a Business Systems Analyst, Sales Systems Lead, or RevOps Systems role, with real ownership of work in a core funnel domain such as lead management, opportunity and pipeline, renewals and account management, or partner channel&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience designing and rolling out a lifecycle, process model, or forecasting motion at a fast-growing company, owning it from discovery through enablement and adoption&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Credibility with GTM stakeholders: you&#39;ve been in the pipeline review, forecast call, or planning session, and you can push back when there&#39;s a better answer&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Hands-on Salesforce skills, with comfort building meaningful parts of your own solution (Flow, validation, assignment and routing, page and Path design) and specs that make the handoff to developers clean&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Crisp communication across GTM teams, leadership, RevOps, and engineers, adjusting altitude for each&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;5+ years of experience in GTM/Revenue systems roles&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Salesforce Administrator certification&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Advanced Administrator, Business Analyst, or Sales Cloud Consultant certification&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience partnering with RevOps or Sales Strategy on team-structure questions (ownership, routing, splits, territory) and turning those decisions into working system design&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience across more than one part of the customer lifecycle, such as lead, opportunity, renewal, or partner&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Curiosity about AI-assisted systems work and eagerness to fold it into how you design, build, and document; prior hands-on use is a strong plus&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;The annual compensation range for this role is listed below.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For sales roles, the range provided is the role’s On Target Earnings (&quot;OTE&quot;) range, meaning that the range includes both the sales commissions/sales bonuses target and annual base salary for the role.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Annual Salary:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$270,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$315,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Logistics&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum education: &lt;/strong&gt;Bachelor’s degree or an equivalent combination of education, training, and/or experience&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required field of study:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;A field relevant to the role as demonstrated through coursework, training, or professional experience&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum years of experience: &lt;/strong&gt;Years of experience required will correlate with the internal job level requirements for the position&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location-based hybrid policy:&lt;/strong&gt; Currently, we expect all staff to be in one of our offices at least 25% of the time. However, some roles may require more time in our offices.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Visa sponsorship:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;We do sponsor visas! However, we aren&#39;t able to successfully sponsor visas for every role and every candidate. But if we make you an offer, we will make every reasonable effort to get you a visa, and we retain an immigration lawyer to help with this.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We encourage you to apply even if you do not believe you meet every single qualification.&lt;/strong&gt; Not all strong candidates will meet every single qualification as listed.&amp;nbsp; Research shows that people who identify as being from underrepresented groups are more prone to experiencing imposter syndrome and doubting the strength of their candidacy, so we urge you not to exclude yourself prematurely and to submit an application if you&#39;re interested in this work. We think AI systems like the ones we&#39;re building have enormous social and ethical implications. We think this makes representation even more important, and we strive to include a range of diverse perspectives on our team.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Your safety matters to us.&lt;/strong&gt; To protect yourself from potential scams, remember that Anthropic recruiters only contact you from&amp;nbsp;@anthropic.com&amp;nbsp;email addresses. In some cases, we may partner with vetted recruiting agencies who will identify themselves as working on behalf of Anthropic. Be cautious of emails from other domains. Legitimate Anthropic recruiters will never ask for money, fees, or banking information before your first day. If you&#39;re ever unsure about a communication, don&#39;t click any links—visit&amp;nbsp;&lt;u data-stringify-type=&quot;underline&quot;&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link c-link--underline&quot; href=&quot;http://anthropic.com/careers&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;http://anthropic.com/careers&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot; data-remove-tab-index=&quot;true&quot;&gt;anthropic.com/careers&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&amp;nbsp;directly for confirmed position openings.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How we&#39;re different&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe that the highest-impact AI research will be big science. At Anthropic we work as a single cohesive team on just a few large-scale research efforts. And we value impact — advancing our long-term goals of steerable, trustworthy AI — rather than work on smaller and more specific puzzles. We view AI research as an empirical science, which has as much in common with physics and biology as with traditional efforts in computer science. We&#39;re an extremely collaborative group, and we host frequent research discussions to ensure that we are pursuing the highest-impact work at any given time. As such, we greatly value communication skills.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The easiest way to understand our research directions is to read our recent research. This research continues many of the directions our team worked on prior to Anthropic, including: GPT-3, Circuit-Based Interpretability, Multimodal Neurons, Scaling Laws, AI &amp;amp; Compute, Concrete Problems in AI Safety, and Learning from Human Preferences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Come work with us!&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anthropic is a public benefit corporation headquartered in San Francisco. We offer competitive compensation and benefits, optional equity donation matching, generous vacation and parental leave, flexible working hours, and a lovely office space in which to collaborate with colleagues. &lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Guidance on Candidates&#39; AI Usage:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Learn about&amp;nbsp;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link&quot; href=&quot;https://www.anthropic.com/candidate-ai-guidance&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://www.anthropic.com/candidate-ai-guidance&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;our policy&lt;/a&gt; for using AI in our application process.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;GitLab is the intelligent orchestration platform for DevSecOps. GitLab enables organizations to increase developer productivity, improve operational efficiency, reduce security and compliance risk, and accelerate digital transformation. More than 50 million registered users and more than 50% of the Fortune 100* trust GitLab to ship better, more secure software faster.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The same principles built into our products are reflected in how our team works: we embrace AI as a core productivity multiplier, with all team members expected to incorporate AI into their daily workflows to drive efficiency, innovation, and impact. GitLab is where careers accelerate, innovation flourishes, and every voice is valued. Our high-performance culture is driven by our values&amp;nbsp;and continuous knowledge exchange, enabling our team members to reach their full potential while collaborating with industry leaders to solve complex problems. &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OuZIb5zszQI&quot;&gt;Co-create the future with us&lt;/a&gt; as we build technology that transforms how the world develops software.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;*&lt;em&gt;Fortune 500® is a registered trademark of Fortune Media IP Limited, used under license. Claim based on GitLab data. Fortune 100 refers to the top 20% ranked companies in the 2025 Fortune 500 list, published in June 2025. Fortune and Fortune Media IP Limited are not affiliated with, and do not endorse products or services of GitLab.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;An overview of this role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Technical Program Manager on GitLab&#39;s all-remote R&amp;amp;D PMO team, you will own complex, end-to-end programs that are central to our AI-powered DevSecOps strategy. You will drive high-priority initiatives across product, engineering, data, and security teams, transforming strategic vision into executable plans that deliver innovative capabilities like the GitLab Duo Agent Platform and next-generation developer tools. You will work closely with executive leaders and cross-functional stakeholders, serving as the bridge between strategy and execution through clear communication, proactive risk management, and structured program delivery. In your first year, you will independently lead strategic programs, driving predictable execution, thoughtful tradeoffs between quality and speed, and transparent stakeholder alignment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Some examples of our projects:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leading the GitLab Duo Agent Platform from GA through enterprise adoption, including customer onboarding, support models, and billing integration for AI-driven capabilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Delivering data-intensive platform initiatives that enhance developer productivity and enterprise analytics capabilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Driving infrastructure modernization and scalability programs that support our growing customer base&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Orchestrating security and compliance initiatives that maintain our industry-leading DevSecOps standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you will do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead end-to-end technical programs across product, engineering, data, and security, from initial scope through launch and continuous improvement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate closely with executive leaders and senior stakeholders to translate strategic vision into actionable roadmaps and align on priorities and tradeoffs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate distributed teams across time zones using strong asynchronous communication, providing structure, clarity, and consistent status updates&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain comprehensive program plans, proactively identifying and mitigating risks and dependencies while facilitating decisions that balance speed, quality, and customer impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with customer success and cross-functional teams to refine communication plans, and operational workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Champion GitLab&#39;s values and culture within programs, fostering collaborative excellence, continuous improvement, and innovation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you will bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience leading technical program initiatives in product, engineering, data, or security environments, with demonstrated success delivering complex programs from inception through scaled adoption&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to define strategy and create clarity within extreme ambiguity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong background in SaaS, cloud infrastructure, or DevOps technology companies, with ability to quickly master the GitLab platform and AI/ML initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience influencing and driving impact at a division and company-wide scale, affecting market position and revenue&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellence in cross-functional leadership, with experience partnering with engineering, product, security teams and engaging effectively with senior and C-level stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Outstanding communication skills, including asynchronous collaboration, executive reporting, and the ability to translate technical complexity into clear business impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of success in fast-paced, dynamic environments with evolving technical requirements and market opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong facilitation and influence skills, with ability to drive consensus across diverse stakeholder groups while building trust through transparency and delivery excellence&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expertise in high-level stakeholder management, including masterful communication with Executive Boards and enterprise Customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborative leadership style aligned with GitLab&#39;s values, including respect, openness to feedback, and commitment to team success&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of redefining organizational operations and serving as an escalation point to resolve highly complex, enterprise-level challenges&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Welcome candidates from diverse backgrounds, including those with consulting, enterprise technology, or technical leadership experience who have owned outcomes and delivered transformational initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to act as a visionary leader, shaping R&amp;amp;D direction and fostering technical excellence across the organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team:&lt;/strong&gt; The Technical Program Management team sits within GitLab&#39;s R&amp;amp;D Program Management Office and drives product, engineering, data, and security initiatives across our AI-powered DevSecOps platform. You will join our growing, distributed team of Technical Program Managers currently spanning North America and Europe. We own the end-to-end delivery of complex, cross-functional programs including AI platform capabilities, enterprise customer initiatives, and strategic technology transformations. As an all-remote team, we excel at asynchronous communication to coordinate across time zones while partnering closely with executive leaders and stakeholders to deliver business-critical outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How GitLab Supports Full-Time Employees&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/total-rewards/benefits/general-and-entity-benefits/&quot;&gt;Benefits to support your health, finances, and well-being&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/people-group/time-off-and-absence/time-off-types/#flexible-paid-time-off-pto&quot;&gt;Flexible Paid Time Off&amp;nbsp;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/company/culture/inclusion/tmrg-tmag/&quot;&gt;Team Member Resource Groups&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/total-rewards/stock-options/&quot;&gt;Equity Compensation &amp;amp; Employee Stock Purchase Plan&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/people-group/learning-and-development/growth-and-development/&quot;&gt;Growth and Development Fund&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/total-rewards/benefits/general-and-entity-benefits/#parental-leave&quot;&gt;Parental Leave&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please note that we welcome interest from candidates with varying levels of experience; many successful candidates do not meet every single requirement. Additionally, studies have shown that people from &lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/company/culture/inclusion/#examples-of-select-underrepresented-groups&quot;&gt;underrepresented groups&lt;/a&gt; are less likely to apply to a job unless they meet every single qualification. If you&#39;re excited about this role, please apply and allow our recruiters to assess your application.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Country Hiring Guidelines: &lt;/strong&gt;GitLab hires new team members in countries around the world. All of our roles are remote, however some roles may carry specific location-based eligibility requirements. Our Talent Acquisition team can help answer any questions about location after starting the recruiting process.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Privacy Policy: &lt;/strong&gt;Please review our &lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/hiring/candidate-faq/recruitment-privacy-policy/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Recruitment Privacy Policy.&lt;/a&gt; Your privacy is important to us.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;GitLab is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and is an affirmative action employer. GitLab’s policies and practices relating to recruitment, employment, career development and advancement, promotion, and retirement are based solely on merit, regardless of race, color, religion, ancestry, sex (including pregnancy, lactation, sexual orientation, gender identity, or gender expression), national origin, age, citizenship, marital status, mental or physical disability, genetic information (including family medical history), discharge status from the military, protected veteran status (which includes disabled veterans, recently separated veterans, active duty wartime or campaign badge veterans, and Armed Forces service medal veterans), or any other basis protected by law. GitLab will not tolerate discrimination or harassment based on any of these characteristics. See also&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/people-policies/inc-usa/#equal-employment-opportunity-policy&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;GitLab’s EEO Policy&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/labor-and-employment-notices/#eeoc-us-equal-employment-opportunity-commission-notices&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;EEO is the Law&lt;/a&gt;. If you have a disability or special need that requires&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/people-policies/inc-usa/#reasonable-accommodation&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;accommodation&lt;/a&gt;, please let us know during the&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/hiring/interviewing/#adjustments-to-our-interview-process&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;recruiting process&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Anthropic&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anthropic’s mission is to create reliable, interpretable, and steerable AI systems. We want AI to be safe and beneficial for our users and for society as a whole. Our team is a quickly growing group of committed researchers, engineers, policy experts, and business leaders working together to build beneficial AI systems.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an AV Operations Specialist, you&#39;ll be accountable for how the AV spaces perform, how support requests get resolved, and how events land in the space you&#39;re responsible for. This role will help own all areas within the AV landscape. In a given week you might execute a preventative maintenance sweep across a floor of conference rooms, work the support queue and drive a recurring failure to root cause, and then run technical coverage for an all-hands or an executive presentation that evening.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll be the regional presence our AV Engineering and Production teams build on — the person who catches problems before users report them, and who turns what you learn on the ground into standards the rest of the team can run from. Your work directly enables the collaboration and transparency that advance our AI safety mission.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Site Ownership &amp;amp; Room Health&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the AV owner for your office — accountable for the health, readiness, and performance of every room and event space in the building&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Execute preventative maintenance programs and recurring room sweeps on a defined cadence, not only in response to tickets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain accurate inventory of room systems, peripherals, wireless microphones, cameras, and portable production gear, including spares strategy and replacement cycles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate AV scope for office moves, room reconfigurations, and new-space readiness in partnership with Workplace and AV Engineering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Know your estate: maintain the room documentation, as-builts, and site-specific gotchas that make your office supportable by anyone on the team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Support Operations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help own the AV support queue — triage, prioritization, resolution, and escalation with clear diagnostic context&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in the regional AV on-run rotation (West, East, or EMEA), covering AV issues during local business hours alongside the daily room-check discipline&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Systematically isolate faults to a point in the signal chain rather than reaching for reboots and cable swaps&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive recurring issues to root cause and surface them to AV Engineering as candidates for platform-level or design-level fixes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to runbooks, standard operating procedures, and knowledge base documentation that other technicians follow&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Event Support &amp;amp; Production&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide technical coverage for live and hybrid events in your office — from small executive presentations and team meetings through to all-hands and company-wide broadcasts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operate event production systems including audio consoles, video switchers, camera systems, playback, and streaming encoders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run pre-event readiness: walkthroughs, rehearsals, source checks, gear staging, and failover planning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Handle scoping conversations with requesters — translating what a stakeholder wants the event to feel like into an equipment and staffing plan that fits the team&#39;s SLA&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turn novel one-off events into repeatable standards — a template, runbook, or gear list that makes the next one easier for the whole team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Vendor Direction &amp;amp; Cross-functional Partnership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct AV integrators, contractors, and event labor on site, holding them to defined scope, SLAs, and quality standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Workplace, Events, and IT on lead times, expectations, and readiness&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the regional feedback loop to AV Engineering — what&#39;s failing, what&#39;s missing, and what the standard should be&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate status, risk, and resolution to non-technical stakeholders in clear, calm, jargon-free language&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You May Be a Good Fit If You:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have 8+ years of hands-on experience in AV operations, workplace technology, or technical event support&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have owned a standing estate — the same rooms, the same stakeholders, week over week — and were accountable for how those spaces performed over time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring working fluency across room systems, event audio, video, camera, and streaming, with enough depth to diagnose problems rather than only report them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are comfortable being the only AV person in the building, and can prioritize independently across maintenance, support, and events&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring structure to ambiguity — checklists, intake processes, maintenance cadences, and documentation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are energized rather than drained by being the front-facing technical partner to executives, event producers, and everyone else who walks up to you in a hallway&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take ownership end-to-end, from noticing a recurring failure to getting it permanently fixed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Thrive in a fast-moving environment where standards are being written rather than inherited&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strong Candidates May Also Have Experience With:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Q-SYS DSP platforms — comfortable navigating and reasoning about existing audio/video routing and control designs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Logitech CollabOS and Sync, Google Meet hardware, Zoom Rooms, and enterprise room system administration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Preventative maintenance and room-sweep programs across a distributed room fleet&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Broadcast video switchers such as Blackmagic ATEM, Ross Carbonite, or NewTek TriCaster&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Digital audio mixing consoles such as Yamaha DM7 or CL/QL series, and Shure wireless systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;PTZ camera systems and multi-camera workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ticketing and workflow systems such as Jira, and participation in an on-run rotation&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinating AV contractors, integrators, and labor for site support and event coverage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CTS certification or equivalent demonstrated capability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Specific Location Policy:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This role will be based in our New York office&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This role is expected to be in office 5 days per week&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Occasional evening and early-morning coverage is expected around major events&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4-6 weeks of travel annually may be expected for this role for distributed support, office buildout support, and event coverage as needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
